      "pot": {
        "content": "```python\ndef solution():\n    # Define variables name and value\n    advertising = [3000, 4000, 5000, 6000, 7000]\n    revenue = [20000, 23000, 25000, 26000, 28000]\n\n    # Do math calculation to get the answer\n    mean_advertising = sum(advertising) / len(advertising)\n    mean_revenue = sum(revenue) / len(revenue)\n    numerator = sum(\n        (x - mean_advertising) * (y - mean_revenue)\n        for x, y in zip(advertising, revenue)\n    )\n    denominator = sum((x - mean_advertising) ** 2 for x in advertising)\n    slope = numerator / denominator\n    answer = round(slope, 2)\n\n    # Return answer\n    return answer\n```",
